1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,094
The relieving watchstander needs
to know what remains unresolved,

2
00:00:05,094 --> 00:00:07,132
and where the evidence is.

3
00:00:07,132 --> 00:00:10,319
Eight Bells is a focused
watch-turnover tool:

4
00:00:10,319 --> 00:00:13,789
it reads the log, flags
what needs a second look,

5
00:00:13,789 --> 00:00:18,179
and drafts the turnover with a
source line behind every point.

6
00:00:18,179 --> 00:00:19,927
Today's log is synthetic.

7
00:00:20,177 --> 00:00:21,912
Here is how it works.

8
00:00:21,912 --> 00:00:26,298
Everything runs on this one computer:
the page in your browser,

9
00:00:26,298 --> 00:00:31,242
a small PowerShell server on loopback,
and a launcher you double-click.

10
00:00:31,242 --> 00:00:32,869
Closing the tab stops the server.

11
00:00:33,569 --> 00:00:38,041
Records live in an encrypted
store for your Windows account,

12
00:00:38,041 --> 00:00:40,426
with a hash-chained audit trail.

13
00:00:41,213 --> 00:00:45,001
Watch logs go in: text, CSV, JSON, tables,

14
00:00:45,001 --> 00:00:48,608
XML, and the text layer of digital PDFs.

15
00:00:49,308 --> 00:00:54,322
Out come findings and a turnover draft,
built offline by rules, with no AI.

16
00:00:54,322 --> 00:00:57,358
Every point links to its line in the log.

17
00:00:58,058 --> 00:01:00,259
An AI briefing is optional.

18
00:01:00,259 --> 00:01:03,551
The model key sits in Lazarette,
shared to Fairlead.

19
00:01:03,551 --> 00:01:06,156
Eight Bells has its own Fairlead key,

20
00:01:06,156 --> 00:01:09,959
and requests stay local-only
unless you say otherwise.

21
00:01:10,659 --> 00:01:14,814
Reviewed lessons can go to
Halyard as a hand-off file,

22
00:01:14,814 --> 00:01:17,584
and counts go to Semaphore as a CSV.

23
00:01:17,584 --> 00:01:21,971
Not built yet: OCR for scans,
and vendor log formats.

24
00:01:22,671 --> 00:01:27,389
And the guardrails: loopback only,
drafts tied to their source,

25
00:01:27,389 --> 00:01:31,807
AI only when you consent,
and every finding needs a person.

26
00:01:32,198 --> 00:01:35,764
To use the AI briefing,
give Eight Bells its own key.

27
00:01:35,764 --> 00:01:41,171
In Fairlead, open Clients,
and choose Install for an app.

28
00:01:41,871 --> 00:01:43,643
Name it EightBells and install.

29
00:01:44,343 --> 00:01:48,217
Fairlead makes the key and saves it
straight to Windows Credential Manager.

30
00:01:48,917 --> 00:01:50,005
It is never shown.

31
00:01:50,705 --> 00:01:54,215
Fairlead's OpenAI connection already
takes its key from Lazarette,

32
00:01:54,215 --> 00:01:56,661
so the provider key never
touches Eight Bells.

33
00:01:57,361 --> 00:02:01,046
Back in Eight Bells, the router
card shows Fairlead answering,

34
00:02:01,046 --> 00:02:02,592
and its own key installed.

35
00:02:02,592 --> 00:02:06,059
Start with an empty store,
and import a log.

36
00:02:06,059 --> 00:02:11,007
This one is a simulated engineering watch,
marked synthetic in its first line.

37
00:02:11,707 --> 00:02:14,854
The preview shows every entry
with its time, its equipment

38
00:02:14,854 --> 00:02:17,729
and its source line number,
before anything is saved.

39
00:02:18,429 --> 00:02:19,968
Import, and it is stored encrypted.

40
00:02:19,968 --> 00:02:22,364
Quality review found
three advisory findings.

41
00:02:22,364 --> 00:02:26,562
They are prompts to check
the record, not conclusions.

42
00:02:27,262 --> 00:02:30,307
The first is an entry out of sequence:

43
00:02:30,307 --> 00:02:34,635
line eight is a late entry,
logged after a later time.

44
00:02:34,635 --> 00:02:36,781
Each finding shows its source lines.

45
00:02:37,481 --> 00:02:40,205
The second is a possible
unresolved condition:

46
00:02:40,205 --> 00:02:43,759
Pump B vibration stays open
from the first line to the last.

47
00:02:43,759 --> 00:02:46,856
A reviewer records a
disposition and a reason.

48
00:02:47,556 --> 00:02:49,753
The review is recorded beside the finding.

49
00:02:50,466 --> 00:02:52,385
The source log is never changed.

50
00:02:52,385 --> 00:02:54,025
Now the turnover, offline.

51
00:02:54,025 --> 00:02:58,277
This browser can reach nothing
but this computer, and AI is off.

52
00:02:58,977 --> 00:03:00,024
Generate the draft.

53
00:03:00,024 --> 00:03:03,256
The rules engine writes it in an instant:

54
00:03:03,256 --> 00:03:07,355
observations, open conditions,
and quality findings.

55
00:03:08,055 --> 00:03:11,314
Select any line number and
the source line opens below,

56
00:03:11,314 --> 00:03:13,151
in the log exactly as imported.

57
00:03:13,151 --> 00:03:15,415
That is the evidence trail.

58
00:03:15,665 --> 00:03:17,197
Now the stale-draft guard.

59
00:03:17,705 --> 00:03:19,329
Generate a draft for this log.

60
00:03:19,946 --> 00:03:22,785
Then the log is corrected,
and a new version is imported.

61
00:03:23,485 --> 00:03:26,449
Select the corrected log
and the old draft is gone.

62
00:03:27,310 --> 00:03:28,770
Copy and Save are disabled.

63
00:03:29,279 --> 00:03:32,188
A draft cannot be exported
once its source has changed.

64
00:03:32,888 --> 00:03:36,147
Even going back to the original
does not bring it back.

65
00:03:36,147 --> 00:03:40,261
Generate again, and the draft is
rebuilt from the source as it is now.

66
00:03:40,261 --> 00:03:44,082
Now the optional AI briefing,
through Fairlead.

67
00:03:44,082 --> 00:03:47,885
The card shows Fairlead answering
and the key installed.

68
00:03:47,885 --> 00:03:52,067
Keep requests on this PC is ticked,
so only local models may answer.

69
00:03:52,767 --> 00:03:56,031
Ask for a draft with
the consent box ticked.

70
00:03:56,031 --> 00:03:58,689
No local model is loaded on this PC,

71
00:03:58,689 --> 00:04:02,528
so Fairlead refuses,
and nothing leaves the machine.

72
00:04:02,528 --> 00:04:03,878
Eight Bells says why.

73
00:04:04,578 --> 00:04:08,528
For synthetic data only,
untick it and name a model.

74
00:04:08,528 --> 00:04:11,954
Fairlead may now use a cloud model,
under that provider's terms.

75
00:04:12,654 --> 00:04:14,865
Same request, now with cloud allowed.

76
00:04:15,565 --> 00:04:19,067
A real answer in about two
seconds, marked unverified,

77
00:04:19,067 --> 00:04:21,986
citing line numbers to
check against the log.

78
00:04:22,686 --> 00:04:27,517
Fairlead's Activity page shows both
calls from the client EightBells:

79
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:31,718
one refused as private,
one served by OpenAI's gpt-4.1-mini.

80
00:04:31,718 --> 00:04:35,909
Across the two logs, Eight Bells
notices that Pump B stays open,

81
00:04:35,909 --> 00:04:37,350
and suggests a lesson.

82
00:04:38,050 --> 00:04:40,437
Save it as a draft, then mark it reviewed.

83
00:04:40,437 --> 00:04:43,543
That mark is local, not a signed approval.

84
00:04:44,243 --> 00:04:45,243
Export it for Halyard.

85
00:04:45,789 --> 00:04:48,138
Halyard's Intake reads
that file through its API.

86
00:04:48,138 --> 00:04:51,182
It returns a story draft
linked back to the lesson.

87
00:04:51,182 --> 00:04:54,671
Preview only, nothing
written to the backlog.

88
00:04:54,671 --> 00:04:57,673
There is no button for
it in Halyard's page yet.

89
00:04:58,373 --> 00:05:02,177
Counts per watch go to Semaphore as a CSV:

90
00:05:02,177 --> 00:05:06,517
logs, open conditions,
findings, lessons. No log text.

91
00:05:06,517 --> 00:05:11,288
That is Eight Bells: a focused
watch-turnover capability.

92
00:05:11,288 --> 00:05:17,064
It tells the relieving watch what
is open, and where the evidence is.

93
00:05:17,064 --> 00:05:21,216
The log was synthetic,
the findings are advisory,

94
00:05:21,216 --> 00:05:24,012
and a person verifies everything.

95
00:05:24,012 --> 00:05:25,012
Fair winds.
